-- lib/mem/sig.cub — memory as a signature (archive/2026-11-11/README.md, "Memory is a signature"), over
-- lib/obs.cub and lib/world.cub.
--
-- A language reader produces a process over MemSig (and its world's signature S) and never
-- touches a memory value. A pointer is MPtr, opaque to readers: they get pointers from
-- commands and give them back to commands. Two handlers interpret the signature:
-- lib/mem/flat.cub (into the machine's memory: what is compiled) and lib/mem/memory.cub (the
-- abstract memory with its checks: the meaning), and lib/mem/memory.cub proves the one theorem
-- relating them, with the refinement relation and its two rules defined here.
import "scalar.hypercubical"
